WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.549
Integrated original scenario: Jordan understands the reason for the shared queue and wants fewer missed handoffs.

00:00:06.789 --> 00:00:12.699
Jordan completes the tutorial accurately but cannot finish a real handoff while answering phones.

00:00:12.939 --> 00:00:16.395
A manager proposes a mandatory repeat of the tutorial.

00:00:17.085 --> 00:00:20.626
First decision: ask Jordan to walk through a recent handoff.

00:00:20.866 --> 00:00:25.069
You learn that the phone interrupts every attempt and there is no shift overlap.

00:00:25.309 --> 00:00:32.178
The earliest evidenced barrier is practical Ability, rather than missing purpose, willingness or procedural knowledge.

00:00:32.418 --> 00:00:37.069
This is a hypothesis based on the facts given, not a diagnosis of Jordan.

00:00:37.759 --> 00:00:44.884
Second decision: agree a short, covered practice period and investigate a workable handoff interval with the shift lead.

00:00:45.124 --> 00:00:47.087
Observe the next realistic attempt.

00:00:47.327 --> 00:00:52.425
If Jordan completes it accurately with coverage, that supports the workload hypothesis.

00:00:52.665 --> 00:00:57.444
If Jordan cannot choose the right action even with time and access, revisit Knowledge.

00:00:58.134 --> 00:01:03.467
Third decision: after initial success, check whether the arrangement survives a busy shift.

00:01:03.707 --> 00:01:05.777
Sustained success needs follow-through.

00:01:06.017 --> 00:01:09.643
Source for focusing on the earliest unmet element: a-r1.

00:01:09.883 --> 00:01:12.891
The scenario sequence and support plan are original.

00:01:13.581 --> 00:01:18.488
Create your own four-part plan: behavior, support, observation and review date.

00:01:18.728 --> 00:01:23.101
Example: “Jordan records an owner and next action on each open ticket.

00:01:23.341 --> 00:01:26.008
The shift lead arranges five minutes of coverage.

00:01:26.248 --> 00:01:35.763
We review one realistic handoff together tomorrow, then discuss whether the approach worked during Friday’s busy shift.” Avoid including real confidential

00:01:35.763 --> 00:01:38.685
employee information in your practice response.

00:01:39.375 --> 00:01:40.463
Now it's your turn.

00:01:40.703 --> 00:01:46.335
Branch decision: after coverage is provided, Jordan completes the practice ticket accurately.

00:01:46.575 --> 00:01:47.471
What next?

00:01:47.711 --> 00:01:50.826
